hadiths[95]{hadithnumber,text}:
"299","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to the people and said: ""O people! Allah has made Hajj obligatory upon you."" A man stood up and asked: ""Is it every year?"" He repeated this three times, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) kept turning away from him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I had said yes, it would have become obligatory, and if it had become obligatory, you would not have been able to do it."" Then he said: ""Leave me as long as I leave you (do not ask me unnecessary questions). Those before you were destroyed only because of their excessive questioning of their prophets and their disagreements with them. When I command you regarding something, do it as much as you are able, and when I forbid you from something, then avoid it."""
"300","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever matters I leave you with, then leave me with them (do not ask me about them). The people before you were destroyed because of asking too many questions of their prophets and differing with them. So when I command you regarding something, act upon it as much as you are able, and when I forbid you from something, then abstain from it."""
"301","It is narrated from Shaibah's Umm Walad (may Allah be pleased with her) that she was performing Sa'i between Safa and Marwah when she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and he was saying: ""The Abtah (valley) can only be crossed by running."""
"302","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs Hajj of this House (the Ka'bah) and does not commit any obscenity nor any sin, he returns free from sins just as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him."""
"303","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): Whoever performs Hajj to this House and does not commit any obscenity or sin, he becomes as free from sins as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him."
"304","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Whoever performs Hajj and does not commit any obscenity or sin, he returns free from sins just as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him."""
"305","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will leave Madinah out of aversion, while Madinah is better for them—if only they knew."""
"306","Muharrir bin Abi Hurairah narrated from his father, who said: I was among those whom the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent with Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) to announce the declaration of Bara’ah in Makkah. His son (Muharrir) asked him: What things would you announce? He said: Four things: Only a believing soul will enter Paradise; after this year, no polytheist will perform Hajj; there will be no naked circumambulation of the House (Ka'bah); and whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), its duration is four months. He said: I used to make this announcement until my voice became hoarse."
"307","The narrator reported: Wakee’ (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us with this chain the same as the previous hadith."
"308","Habibah bint Abi Tajrah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing Sa’i between Safa and Marwah, and he was saying: “Allah has made Sa’i obligatory upon you, so perform Sa’i.” Due to his brisk running, his garment and lower wrap were swirling around his shins until I could see his knees."
"309","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) uttering only these words on the occasion of Hajj and Umrah: ""Here I am, O Allah! Here I am, You have no partner, here I am, all praise and blessings are Yours."" Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that in this, Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""And sovereignty as well, You have no partner."""
"310","Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: She used to set out (for Hajj) with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and before entering into Ihram, musk perfume would be applied to her. Then she would perspire, and its effect would be visible on her face. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would see her and he would not forbid her from this."
"311","Sulaiman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas narrated from his mother, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) at Jamrah Aqabah on the day of sacrifice (10th Dhul-Hijjah), and he was saying: ""O people! Do not kill one another, and pelt the Jamrah with pebbles like the size of a date stone."" Then he pelted the Jamrah and did not stand by it, and moved on. Others besides Jarir narrated from Yazid with this chain, that a man was shielding the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) from the people. I asked about him, and I was told he was Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he was saying: ""O people! Do not crowd."" And in it is mentioned: Then he came to the valley and pelted again."
"312","Yazid bin Abi Ziyad narrated with the same chain a hadith similar to that of Jarir."
"313","Sayyidah Umm al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us in the plain of Arafat, then she mentioned the like of it."
"314","Sayyida Umm al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: He (peace be upon him) supplicated three times for those who shaved their heads (during Hajj and Umrah). Each time, it was requested of him: And those who trim their hair (pray for them as well), so on the third time he said: ""And for those who trim their hair as well."""
"315","Lady Umm al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying the same."
"316","Lady Umm Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I intended to perform Umrah in Ramadan, while her husband had given the she-camel in the way of Allah. I mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give it to her, for performing Umrah in Ramadan (in terms of reward and merit) is equal to Hajj."""
"317","Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman bin Harith bin Hisham narrated from a woman of the Ashja‘ tribe (Umm Ma‘qil, may Allah be pleased with her) that she intended to perform ‘Umrah in Ramadan, while her husband had a camel which he had given in the way of Allah. She mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: “Give it to her, for performing ‘Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to performing Hajj.”"
"318","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “There is no migration (hijrah) after this day (from Makkah), but jihad (migration for jihad) and intention remain, and when you are called to go out (for jihad), then go out.” And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “This city—Allah made it sacred from the very day He created the heavens and the earth, so it is sacred by Allah’s sanctity until the Day of Resurrection. Fighting in it was not made lawful for anyone before me, and it was made lawful for me only for a part of a day, so it is sacred by Allah’s sanctity until the Day of Resurrection. Its grass is not to be cut, nor its thorn to be cut, nor its game to be chased, nor is its lost property to be picked up except by one who will announce it.” Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Except for idhkhir (a type of grass), because it is for their blacksmiths and for their houses (roofs), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Except for idhkhir (it is permissible to cut it).”"
"319","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) the same like, he said: ""Its fallen item will not be picked up except by one who will announce it."""
"320","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man came to Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""No man should sit in seclusion with a woman except that her mahram relative is with her."""
"321","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them): The people, after completing the rites of Hajj, would return (to their respective homelands and regions) from every direction. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them: ""That their last act should be (to spend time in) circumambulation at the House of Allah (the Ka'bah)."""
"322","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that it was commanded that their last moments be spent at the House of Allah (performing Tawaf), except for a menstruating woman, because she has been granted permission or concession."
"323","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: I never saw that anyone opposed Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and he left him until he made him acknowledge (the truth). So Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) disagreed with him regarding the issue of the woman who gets her menses after performing the Tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice (10th Dhul-Hijjah). Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: She may depart. Then he sent a message to the woman who had faced this situation during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and that woman agreed with the stance of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"324","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The people were commanded that their last act should be at the House of Allah (by performing the Farewell Tawaf), except that a concession was given to menstruating women, except that a concession was given to menstruating women. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated, we say: She will perform the Tawaf of the House of Allah (because the hadith is): ""Until their last act is at the House of Allah."""
"325","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: There was a disagreement between Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas and Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding a menstruating woman departing without performing the Farewell Tawaf. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: She may depart. Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said: She may not depart until she performs Tawaf of the House of Allah. So Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) went to Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and asked her about the issue. She said: She may depart. Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) came out smiling and was saying, ""The ruling is as you (Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both) said: that she may depart."""
"326","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Hatim is a part of the House of Allah, because Allah Almighty has said: ""Perform Tawaf of the Ancient House."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Tawaf from outside the Hatim."
"327","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There are five animals that are wicked; they may be killed even in the Haram, and a person in the state of Ihram may also kill them: the rat, the scorpion, the biting dog, the kite, and the crow."""
"328","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to recite the Talbiyah until the stoning of the Jamrah on the day of sacrifice."
"329","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The circumambulation of the House of Allah is like prayer, except that you can talk during it, so speak only good and virtuous words."""
"330","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that Duba’ah bint Zubair bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with her) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: “I am a heavy-bodied woman, and I intend to perform Hajj. What do you command me?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Enter into the state of Ihram for Hajj, and stipulate a condition that I will come out of Ihram wherever I am prevented (from proceeding).”"
"331","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted Duba’ah (may Allah be pleased with her) to perform Hajj and to stipulate the condition: (O Allah!) Wherever You restrain me, I will come out of Ihram there."
"332","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed Dhu’l-Hulaifah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfah for the people of Syria, Qarn for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and said: “And whoever lives within the miqat, he may begin (ihram) from wherever he wishes (i.e., from whichever place he wishes to enter into ihram).”"
"333","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed Dhu’l-Hulaifa as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfa for the people of Syria, and Yalamlam or Al-Malam for the people of Yemen, and said: “These are the miqats for the people of those places, and for anyone whose family lives within these miqats, he may set out from wherever he wishes (and assume ihram from there).” And he said: “These (miqats) are for the residents of those places and also for those who are not residents but pass through them, until they reach the people of Makkah.”"
"334","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prescribed the Miqat, and the narrator mentioned similarly, and said: And as for the residents of the city who live within the Miqat, they may assume Ihram from wherever they wish."
"335","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed raml (walking briskly) while circumambulating the House of Allah and while performing sa’i between Safa and Marwah, so that the polytheists could see him, because the polytheists had said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions have become weak (and the climate of Madinah has made them weak). So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed raml, in order to show them his strength."
"336","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a man while performing Tawaf of the Ka'bah, who had a ring in his nose and another man was guiding him (making him perform Tawaf). So the Prophet cut it off with his blessed hand, then ordered him to hold him by his hand."
"337","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married Sayyidah Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while he was in the state of Ihram."
"338","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married Sayyidah Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while he was in the state of Ihram. (The Prophet, peace be upon him, had cupping done and medicine put in his nose while in the state of Ihram.)"
"339","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married her, that is, Sayyida Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), while he (peace and blessings be upon him) was in the state of Ihram. Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and Sa'id bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) used to deny this."
"340","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married Sayyidah Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while he was in the state of ihram, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) consummated the marriage with her at the place of Sarif when he was not in the state of ihram."
"341","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) came, so Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to him, while reminding him: How did you tell me that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was in the state of Ihram, meat was gifted to him? So he said to him: Yes, a portion of game meat, so he returned it and said: ""We will not eat it, because we are in the state of Ihram."""
"342","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Sa'b bin Jaththamah (may Allah be pleased with him) presented the meat of a wild donkey as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was in the state of Ihram, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned it. When he saw signs of sadness and displeasure on his face, he said: ""We do not return your gift except that we are in the state of Ihram."""
"343","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he was asked (on the occasion of Hajj) about offering sacrifice, shaving the head, and the order of performing the stoning of the Jamarat, whether they could be done earlier or later, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm."""
"344","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that a questioner asked him, so he said: I shaved my head before slaughtering the sacrificial animal. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Slaughter (now), there is no harm."" He said: I performed Tawaf before Rami. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(Now) perform Rami, there is no harm."""
"345","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: In the days of ignorance, performing ‘Umrah during the months of Hajj was considered the greatest immorality (sinful act). They used to say: When the back of the camel becomes rested, its hair grows well, and the month of Safar ends, then it becomes lawful for the one performing ‘Umrah to do so. So, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions came in the morning of the fourth (of Dhul-Hijjah) in the state of Ihram for Hajj, and he commanded them to intend to open their Ihram for ‘Umrah. This was hard on them, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, what has become lawful for us? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Everything has become lawful.”"
"346","Wahb narrated with this chain in a similar manner, Yahya (may Allah have mercy on him) stated, because he was only familiar with ‘Umrah. Did you not see that he used to say: We only consider Hajj."
"347","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fixed Dhu’l-Hulaifah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfah for the people of Syria, Qarn al-Manazil for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and he said: “These are (the miqat) for the people of those places and also for those who are not residents of those places but pass through them. These are the miqat for those performing Hajj and ‘Umrah. Whoever’s family lives within the miqat, then he may enter into ihram from wherever he wishes, even the people of Makkah will enter into ihram from within Makkah itself.”"
"348","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fixed Dhu’l-Hulaifa as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfa for the people of Syria, Qarn for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen. These are for the residents of those places and also for those who are not their residents but pass through them. These are for anyone who intends to perform Hajj or Umrah. And whoever’s residence is within the boundaries of the miqat, he should enter into ihram from his own house, even the people of Makkah from Makkah itself (should enter into ihram)."
"349","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Listen! No man should sit in seclusion with a woman except that there is a mahram relative with her, and no woman should travel except that there is a mahram relative with her.” A man said: O Messenger of Allah! My name has been written for such-and-such battle, while my wife is going for Hajj. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Go and perform Hajj with your wife.”"
"350","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No woman should travel unless she is accompanied by a mahram relative."" In his narration, Amr narrated from Abu Ma'bad that a man said: O Messenger of Allah! My name has been registered for such-and-such battle, while my wife is going for Hajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go, perform Hajj with her."""
"351","Abdur Rahman bin Abi Mulaika narrated: A man came to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), so he asked: Where have you come from? He replied: I have drunk the water of Zamzam. He (Ibn Abbas) said: Did you drink it in the manner it should be drunk? He replied: How should it be drunk? He said: When you intend to drink the water of Zamzam, face the Qiblah, then say Bismillah, then drink it in three breaths, then fill yourself with it, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The difference between us and the hypocrites is that they do not fill themselves with the water of Zamzam (they do not drink much of it)."""
"352","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent some members of his family and their belongings (to Mina) on the night of Muzdalifah, and I was among them."
"353","Hazrat Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted people to depart from Muzdalifah to Mina in the last part of the night. Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to send his son, while he was still a child, (from Muzdalifah at night), until he would lead him in the Fajr prayer at Mina."
"354","Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to send his son, while he was still a child, (from Muzdalifah at night) until he would make him perform the Fajr prayer in Mina."
"355","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The entire plain of Arafat is a place of standing (for Hajj), but do not stay in ‘Urnah (a place near Arafat); the entire Muzdalifah is a place of standing, but do not stand in Muhassir (a place between Mina and Muzdalifah); and all the roads of Makkah are places for sacrifice."""
"356","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: In the days of ignorance, Dhu al-Majaz and ‘Ukaz were commercial centers. When Islam came, it was as if they disliked (trading during the days of Hajj), so Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: « لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلًا مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ » ""There is no sin upon you that you seek the bounty of your Lord."" That is, (do trade) during the months of Hajj."
"357","Ibn Jurayj narrated: ‘Ata’ (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked about a person in the state of ihram—can he buy and sell? He said: They used to avoid it, until this verse was revealed: « لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلًا مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ » “There is no sin upon you that you seek the bounty of your Lord.” That is, during the months of Hajj."
"358","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""This is the ‘Umrah from which we have benefited, so whoever does not have a sacrificial animal should come out of ihram."" It was asked to him, what kind of coming out of ihram is meant? (i.e., from which restrictions of ihram is one exempted?) He (peace be upon him) said: ""All matters (which were forbidden due to ihram) have become permissible."" He said: ""‘Umrah has been included in Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."" Ishaq (may Allah have mercy on him) said: That is, performing ‘Umrah in the months of Hajj is permissible until the Day of Resurrection, and this is because the people of the Age of Ignorance did not consider it permissible to perform ‘Umrah in the months of Hajj."
"359","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions came to perform Hajj, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! End your state of Ihram, except for the one who has a sacrificial animal with him. If I had known what I know now, I would not have done this. Umrah has been incorporated into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."""
"360","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) shaved his head during his Hajj, so some of the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them all) shaved their heads while others trimmed their hair. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! And those who trim their hair? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! And those who trim their hair? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave their heads."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! And those who trim their hair? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And those who trim their hair."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! What is the matter with those who shave their heads? Why did you express mercy for them? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Because they did not show any doubt (and followed me by shaving their heads)."""
"361","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to kiss the Yemeni Corner and place his cheek upon it."
"362","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: They used to dislike including trade in their Hajj until this verse was revealed: « لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلًا مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ » ""There is no sin upon you that you seek the bounty of your Lord."""
"363","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: During the days of Hajj, they used to refrain from buying and selling and trade. They used to say, ""These are days of remembrance."" So Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: « لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلًا مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ » ""There is no sin upon you that you seek the bounty of your Lord."""
"364","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to recite the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrah Aqabah."
"365","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) proclaimed the Talbiyah for ‘Umrah until he touched the Black Stone, and he proclaimed the Talbiyah for Hajj until he stoned the Jamrah."
"366","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to recite the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"367","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: I returned from Muzdalifah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) twice; he would return and tranquility would be upon him."
"368","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had cupping done while in the state of ihram."
"369","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: (At the time of departing from Makkah) there is no special significance to sleeping or staying in the valley of Muhassab; it is merely a place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed."
"370","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent him with wealth and belongings towards Mina on the night of Muzdalifah."
"371","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: No (pilgrim) was permitted to spend the night away from Mina (in Makkah), except Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him), and this permission was granted to him because he used to provide water to the pilgrims."
"372","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) granted Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) permission to spend the nights of Mina in Mecca because he used to provide water to the pilgrims."
"373","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to a woman from the Ansar: The narrator said, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) also mentioned the name of that woman, but I have forgotten it: ""Will you not perform Hajj with us this year?"" She replied: O Messenger of Allah! We had two camels for bringing water, so Abu Fulan and his son (my husband and son) have gone away riding on one camel, and they have left one camel for us, on which we bring water. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the next year comes, perform Umrah in Ramadan, for Umrah in Ramadan is equal to Hajj."""
"374","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me at the time of suhoor from Muzdalifah towards Mina along with his belongings and women, etc. The narrator said: I said to Ata: Have you heard that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: He sent me at night? He replied: No, but at the time of suhoor. Likewise, I said that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: We performed the stoning before Fajr, so where did you pray the Fajr prayer? He replied: No, does that not guide you regarding your suhoor?"
"375","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""My father is an old man; can I perform Hajj on his behalf?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell me, if he had a debt, would you pay it off for him?"" He replied: ""Yes!"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then perform Hajj on his behalf."""
"376","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him), a man said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): I have vowed to sacrifice my own life. So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: For you, in the life of the Messenger of Allah, is the best example. (And in the Noble Qur'an it is stated:) ""And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice."""
"377","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from Makkah, he said: ""Indeed, you are the most beloved of Allah's cities to Allah, and if your inhabitants had not expelled me, I would not have left. O Banu Abd Manaf! If you are granted guardianship over it, then do not prevent any circumambulator at any time of the day or night. If it were not that the Quraysh would become boastful, I would have informed them of the status that is theirs with Allah regarding this place. O Allah! Just as You have provided us with sustenance... (You punished their predecessors and bestowed gifts upon those who came after them.)"""
"378","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: Whoever performs Tawaf of the House of Allah, whether he is performing Hajj or not, becomes free from the restrictions of Ihram. The narrator says: I asked Ata: On what basis did he say this? He replied: On the basis of Allah’s statement « ثُمَّ مَحِلُّهَا إِلَى الْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيقِ » . I asked: Is this after returning from there? He said: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: It is both before and after returning, and he also said this on the basis of the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), because on the occasion of Hajjatul Wada’, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) told the companions to come out of the state of Ihram, and he said this several times."
"379","Ibn Jurayj narrated from Ata from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) a similar narration."
"380","Hazrat Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he mentioned the same example from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"381","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Abu Talib used to send his children and would send Muhammad (peace be upon him) with them when he was young. They used to bring stones for him, and Muhammad (peace be upon him) had a small cloak with white and black stripes, which he would place on his neck. He picked up two small stones (both stones fell from him), and he fainted. When he regained consciousness, he tied his cloak. His cousins said to him: ""What happened to you?"" He replied: ""I have been forbidden from being naked."""
"382","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to stand with his cousins, while they were young, near the Ka'bah, by the idol whose name was Isaf. Then Muhammad (peace be upon him) raised his head towards the back of the Ka'bah, so his cousins said to him: What is the matter with you? He (peace be upon him) said: ""I have been forbidden to stand by the idol."""
"383","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: Adam (peace be upon him) descended wiping his tears at the Black Stone; that stone was whiter than cotton, (its blackness is due to the sins of the people of ignorance) and since he left Paradise, his tears have not dried until he returned to it."
"384","Abu al-Tufail (Amir bin Wathilah bin Amr) (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing Tawaf of the Ka'bah on a camel when I was a boy; he (peace be upon him) was touching the Black Stone with his staff."
"385","Abu al-Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I said to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): The people of your tribe have said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ramal (walking briskly) during tawaf, and that it is a sunnah. He replied: They are right and they are wrong. Fitr narrated from Abu al-Tufail from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: They are right that he performed ramal, and they are wrong that it is a sunnah."
"386","Abu Al-Tufail narrated: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about ramal, and I said: The people of your tribe say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ramal. He replied: They have spoken the truth and they have spoken incorrectly. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came (to Mecca), the polytheists began to say that you (peace and blessings be upon him) and your noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them) had become weak (after going to Madinah), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered them (the noble companions, may Allah be pleased with them) to perform ramal."
"387","Abu al-Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that I said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): The people of your tribe say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ramal and that it is a Sunnah. He replied: They have spoken the truth and they have lied. I asked: What is it that they have spoken the truth about and what is it that they have lied about? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ramal because the Quraysh said: Leave them until they die in the same cave in which they have been besieged. So when the next year came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Makkah while the polytheists were on the side of Qaiqan (mountain). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them to perform ramal (walk briskly with shoulders moving) in three circuits of the House (Ka'bah), so they performed ramal up to the Rukn, and this is not a Sunnah. I said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): The people of your tribe say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed sa'i between Safa and Marwah on a camel and that it is a Sunnah. He replied: They have spoken the truth and have said something incorrect, because when the rites of Hajj were explained to Ibrahim (peace be upon him), Satan confronted him at seven places. So he competed with him, but Ibrahim (peace be upon him) outpaced him, and Jibril (peace be upon him) took him to the Jamrah, where Satan confronted him, so he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he went away. Then he came between the Jamrah and the middle Jamrah, so he pelted him with seven pebbles, and he went away. Then he laid Ismail (peace be upon him) down on his forehead, and there was a white cloth on him, because besides that garment, there was no other cloth that would suffice him. So he said: Take it off me so that you may wrap me in it. While they were taking it off, a voice called out: ""O Ibrahim! You have fulfilled the vision. Thus do We reward the doers of good."" Suddenly, they saw there a white ram with big eyes and horns, so he slaughtered it. Then he went to the Jamrah al-Quswa and pelted it with seven pebbles. Then he brought them to Mina and said: This is the place for people to make their camels kneel. Then he brought them to Muzdalifah and said: This is the Sacred Monument (Mash'ar al-Haram). Then he brought them to Arafat and said: Do you know why it is called 'Arafah (Arafat)? Then he said: Do you know how the Talbiyah was? Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was commanded to proclaim Hajj among the people. The settlements were raised for them and the mountains were lowered with their peaks, so he proclaimed Hajj among the people."
"388","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: When Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was commanded to proclaim Hajj among the people, the settlements were raised for him and the mountains were lowered, so he said: O people! Accept the call of your Lord, so they accepted it."
"389","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came for the ‘Umrah of Hudaybiyyah, he said: “They (the polytheists) will see you tomorrow, so let them see strength and firmness in you.” The narrator stated: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) walked briskly, and they also walked briskly with him until they reached the Yemeni Corner, then walked normally until they reached the Black Stone, then walked briskly until they reached the Yemeni Corner. He did this three times (in three circuits), and then completed four circuits walking normally."
"390","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: We used to call the water of Zamzam ""Shiba'ah"" (that which satisfies hunger), and we used to say that it is the best supporter for the family."
"391","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted a person in the state of Ihram to wear such a colored garment on which there is neither a mark of saffron nor is its color faded."
"392","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Tawaf of the House of Allah on a camel. He had a curved staff with which he touched the Black Stone. When he had completed seven circuits, he prayed two rak‘ahs. Then he came to the place of providing water and asked for water. Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: O Messenger of Allah! Should we not arrange for you the same thing as we do in our homes? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “No, rather give me to drink from where the other people are drinking.” So water (Zamzam) was presented to him and he drank from it."
"393","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Tawaf of the House of Allah on a camel, and when he came to the corner (Rukn), he pointed towards it."
